%U A400464 26,27,28,28,28,29,29,29,30,30,31,31,31,31
%N A400464 Maximum size of a subset of {1, ..., n} whose products of two distinct elements are all distinct.
%C A400464 This is F(n) in Erdős Problem 425.
%H A400464 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/425">Erdős Problem 425</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A400464 a(n-1) <= a(n) <= a(n-1) + 1 for n >= 2.
%F A400464 If p is prime, a(p) = a(p-1) + 1.
%e A400464 a(6) = 5, attained by {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, whose pairwise products are 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20. The whole set {1, ..., 6} does not work since 1*6 = 2*3.
%Y A400464 Cf. A000720, A401472.
%K A400464 nonn,new
%O A400464 1,2
%A A400464 _Seiichi Manyama_, Oct 26 2026
